From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:21:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: test the write callback in fetchIO_write()

fetchIO_write() guarded on f->io_read before calling through
f->io_write, so a fetchIO created with a read callback but no write
callback would dereference a NULL function pointer.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
---
 libfetch/common.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfetch/common.c b/libfetch/common.c
index 3ad0385..26c56e3 100644
--- a/libfetch/common.c
+++ b/libfetch/common.c
@@ -1199,7 +1199,7 @@ fetchIO_read(fetchIO *f, void *buf, size_t len)
 ssize_t
 fetchIO_write(fetchIO *f, const void *buf, size_t len)
 {
-	if (f->io_read == NULL)
+	if (f->io_write == NULL)
 		return EBADF;
 	return (*f->io_write)(f->io_cookie, buf, len);
 }
